experiment: dirbudget
  instrument        dirbudget   trial seed 000000000135fc89   2428 teaching trials at rung 1
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  INDEX SOURCE 4, inherited from the genome and NOT set by dirbudget.
  The index reads the AUDITORY module, so a CtxDrive injected into the
  context module is IGNORED by it -- such an arm is DERIVED, not an
  oracle.
  An "oracle" arm is only an oracle when the drive and the index use the
  SAME module: ctx_match reads 1.000 for a genuine host-written index and
  well below it for a derived one.
  the question      REWARD buys the F1 magnitude and the LESSON buys the
                    direction (echoname, 36 creatures: yoked +29.3 Hz of
                    spread with direction AT ITS OWN NULL; taught - yoked
                    +0.1899 in direction, 6.7 SE, and 1.0 SE in spread).
                    The magnitude's budget curve is CLOSED -- ctxscale
                    saturates at ~118 Hz, 94% of asymptote. Does the
                    ROTATION saturate too, or is it still compute-bound?
  the design        FOUR budgets, one arm each, all TAUGHT. Every argument
                    to the session is echoname's taught arm including the
                    echo buffer, so the arms differ in TICKS AND NOTHING
                    ELSE. Rungs: 3.4M / 6.8M / 13.6M / 27.2M.
  why four          ctxscale's first read was on THREE points and printed
                    COMPUTE-LIMITED; the fourth REVERSED it. Per-doubling
                    ratios 1.98, 1.38, 1.23 -- the exponent halves every
                    doubling, so a three-point ladder on this curve lies
                    with confidence. Three rungs is not a cheaper version
                    of this run, it is a wrong one.
  the primary       `direction` MINUS each creature's OWN null, meaned over
                    36, at each rung -- and the per-doubling RATIO of that
                    excess. Ratios falling to ~1.0 = saturating; ratios
                    holding near 2.0 = compute-limited. The per-creature
                    null is mandatory, not decorative: k-word naming reads
                    0.30 on an EMPTY voice, so chance is not 1/k.
  the free control  rung 1 is 6800000 ticks, so it must reproduce the
                    taught `direction` and `its null` columns of
                    results/echoname-sep-full.log BIT-IDENTICALLY on all
                    36 seeds -- same seed rule (header.seed + r*7919),
                    same arguments. If it does not, this instrument
                    measures something else and the ladder is VOID
                    rather than merely suspect.
  what refuses it   the excess flat across 8x of budget. Then the rotation
                    is architecture-bound exactly as the magnitude is, and
                    budget is closed for BOTH halves of the split. What
                    would establish it: a ratio sequence that has not
                    fallen to ~1.0 by the 27.2M rung.
  stated up front   n = 36 per rung, and this reads a DIFFERENCE of two
                    noisy quantities. A 2-3 SE rung-to-rung step is a
                    HYPOTHESIS in this project; three have been retracted.
                    The SATURATION SHAPE is what this run is for, and that
                    is read off four points at once, not off one step.

